# Line endings.
#
# Without this file nothing normalizes: `core.autocrlf` was unset, and a checkout
# touched from Windows converted 1,116 tracked files to CRLF. That is not cosmetic —
# a CRLF `scripts/update.sh` fails outright on Linux ("syntax error near unexpected
# token $'{\r'"), which is the self-host auto-update path, and every commit made from
# such a tree buries its real diff under ~1,100 line-ending-only files.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) forces LF in the working tree on every platform, so
# shell scripts and Docker entrypoints stay executable wherever they are checked out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.stl    binary
*.3mf    binary
*.step   binary
